 "substitutedBy": null,
 "summary": "Designates criminal investigators employed by the United States transportation security administration's investigations division as peace officers.",
 "title": "Relates to designating certain criminal investigators as peace officers",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "A11185",
     "basePrintNoStr": "A11185-2017",
     "printNo": "A11185",
     "session": 2017,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 349\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bills:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 985, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the criminal procedure law, in relation to security\n      services in the courts\"\n \nAssembly Bill Number 6928-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the criminal procedure law, in relation to desig-\n      nating uniformed court officers in the town of Ossining, county of\n      Westchester as peace officers\"\n \nAssembly Bill Number 11185, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the criminal procedure law, in relation to  persons\n      designated as peace officers\"\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 8176, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the criminal procedure law, in relation to desig-\n      nating court attendants employed by the town of  Somers  as  peace\n      officers\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  Assembly  Bill  No.  985  would create peace officer status for Monroe\ncounty sheriff's officers serving as court security deputies  at  Monroe\ncounty  court  facilities.  Assembly  Bill No. 6928-A would create peace\nofficer status for town of Ossining employees serving as uniformed court\nofficers in the courts of the town of Ossining. Assembly Bill No.  11185\nwould create peace officer status for criminal investigators employed by\nthe  United  States  Transportation  Security  Administration's Investi-\ngations Division. Senate Bill No. 8176 would create peace officer status\nfor employees of the town of Somers serving as court attendants at  town\nof  Somers  court  facilities.  If  designated  as peace officers, these\nemployees would have many of the same powers as police  officers.  Those\npowers  include  the  use  of force to make arrests, the ability to make\nwarrantless arrests and conduct warrantless searches, and the ability to\nissue appearance tickets.\n \n  These bills suffer from the same policy concerns as the  multitude  of\nbills  seeking  to  grant peace officer status to local officials that I\nhave previously vetoed over the past seven years (see, Veto  No.  33  of\n2011,  Veto No. 185 of 2012, Veto No. 228 of 2013, Veto No. 524 of 2014,\nVeto No. 289 of 2015, and Veto Nos. 216 and 226 of 2017).  My  reasoning\nfor  doing  so has not changed - we should not authorize new peace offi-\ncers in a patchwork, ad hoc manner.  The  Legislature  has  provided  no\njustification  for  doing so. Even more, in years past I called upon the\nLegislature to propose a comprehensive, statewide process for  determin-\n \ning which categories of officials may require the law enforcement powers\nthat  are  given to peace officers. When no proposal was provided by the\nLegislature, the Executive took up this responsibility and proposed just\nsuch  a  comprehensive solution. Despite indications that the bill would\nbe taken up during last  year's  legislative  session,  the  Legislature\nnever voted on the Executive's bill.\n \n  I  remain  willing  to  discuss  my  proposal with the Legislature, or\nalternatively, discuss any solution that would address this issue within\nthe broader context of  the  law  enforcement  needs  in  municipalities\nthroughout  the  State.  But  until then, I am once again constrained to\nveto these bills.\n \n  These bills are disapproved.                (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
